1
00:00:21,479 --> 00:00:24,149
TOKYO

2
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,465
Mom! Dad!

3
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:55,180
I'm scared. Mom!

4
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,431
Help me!

5
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:59,434
Please let me go!

6
00:02:19,639 --> 00:02:23,101
THE BLUE ROAD

7
00:02:25,228 --> 00:02:27,271
BOYS' HIGH JUMP
JUNIOR HIGH DIVISION

8
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,190
FIRST PLACE, INOSE HIROSHI

9
00:02:52,964 --> 00:02:54,173
Hello?

10
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:57,010
<i>Sir, we received word
of a murder in Shinjuku.</i>

11
00:02:57,510 --> 00:03:00,555
<i>We need you here ASAP.
The crime scene has been secured.</i>

12
00:03:01,055 --> 00:03:02,390
Okay, got it.

13
00:03:20,325 --> 00:03:22,409
- No photos!
- What the hell, can I get through?

14
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:25,245
Whoa! Something crazy must have happened!

15
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:27,665
No photos allowed. Put your cameras away.

16
00:03:28,249 --> 00:03:30,543
Hey, don't push! Behind the barricade.

17
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,086
Stay calm.

18
00:03:33,087 --> 00:03:35,715
I said no photos.

19
00:03:36,382 --> 00:03:39,510
Hey, I said no photos. Stop!

20
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:43,181
I just wanna go home.

21
00:03:44,432 --> 00:03:46,517
Stop. Everyone, stay back.

22
00:03:49,562 --> 00:03:50,730
Excuse me, sir.

23
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:52,981
Stay behind the line.

24
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:55,442
Uh, Investigation Division One.

25
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:57,361
Oh. Um, may I see your ID first?

26
00:03:57,362 --> 00:04:00,907
My ID? Uh, I left it. You really need it?

27
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:02,783
Yeah.

28
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:04,494
Stand aside.

29
00:04:05,161 --> 00:04:06,913
- Oh, okay. What?
- You idiot.

30
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:09,832
Don't let anyone in
without checking their ID.

31
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:11,542
Apologies.

32
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:14,378
Who's managing this crime scene anyway?

33
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:15,672
Oh, I am, sir.

34
00:04:18,841 --> 00:04:20,926
What the hell are you guys doing out here?

35
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:23,012
I... I... I'm so sorry, sir.

36
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:25,431
Do another sweep, just in case.

37
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:27,516
I'm gonna put the bag over here.

38
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:29,060
Yes, sir, understood.

39
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:33,814
Do you remember
that fire from two years ago,

40
00:04:33,815 --> 00:04:35,816
where a bunch of people died?

41
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:38,861
This was one of the buildings.
It was abandoned afterwards.

42
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:43,031
The officers who confirmed the body
are from the Haramachi Police Station.

43
00:04:43,032 --> 00:04:45,994
We haven't yet been able
to trace who made the report.

44
00:04:47,036 --> 00:04:48,787
ONE FEAR BREEDS INFINITE FEAR

45
00:04:48,788 --> 00:04:50,832
AND ALL METHODS
SHALL BE CONCEALED

46
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:54,794
It's in Korean.

47
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:56,546
What does it say?

48
00:04:57,422 --> 00:04:59,382
We've got an expert on their way.

49
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:02,218
Why didn't you call them sooner?

50
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:03,928
Apologies.

51
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:20,611
Okay. One last pass over everything.

52
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:28,493
Has she been ID'd?

53
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:31,621
Not yet. Female.
Between late teens and early 20s.

54
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:35,292
Time of death is estimated to be
at least 24 hours ago.

55
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:36,626
No sign of sexual assault,

56
00:05:36,627 --> 00:05:39,379
but there are traces
of an unknown drug in her system.

57
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:41,299
At least a hundred milligrams.

58
00:05:42,216 --> 00:05:44,885
So all her limbs were broken
when she was still alive?

59
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:47,263
- Not after she'd been killed?
- That's right.

60
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:50,265
Could something like that
be done with your bare hands?

61
00:05:50,266 --> 00:05:52,726
That would require
an insane amount of strength.

62
00:05:52,727 --> 00:05:56,522
It looks like... a device of sorts was used.

63
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:59,484
A device, huh?

64
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:16,875
- Sir.
- Hmm?

65
00:06:16,876 --> 00:06:18,252
Something wrong?

66
00:06:18,753 --> 00:06:21,506
Mmm. No, nothing. Let's go.

67
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:33,851
I'm assuming
this didn't come from our murderer.

68
00:06:36,521 --> 00:06:37,605
Bean sprouts?

69
00:06:38,231 --> 00:06:40,233
Kimchi? Or <i>yakiniku?</i>

70
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:42,984
You haven't traced the guy
who called it in?

71
00:06:42,985 --> 00:06:46,571
Afraid not. We'll spread the word,
interview the homeless around here.

72
00:06:46,572 --> 00:06:49,408
And what kind of homeless guy
eats grilled meat?

73
00:06:49,409 --> 00:06:51,452
Yes, okay.

74
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:56,581
This building is perfect
for a junkie hangout.

75
00:06:56,582 --> 00:07:00,001
One of them could've called it in fast
and then ran for the hills.

76
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:03,089
Yes, of course.
I'll look for them immediately.

77
00:07:03,756 --> 00:07:05,341
- Hey, excuse me.
- Mmm.

78
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:07,968
What are you doing?

79
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:09,929
Hey, is that a camera?

80
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:12,557
Mind if I take a quick look at it?

81
00:07:13,141 --> 00:07:15,143
Oh, Christ, another reporter.

82
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:18,146
Hey! You listening? Hurry it up already.

83
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:21,274
Hmm.

84
00:07:22,942 --> 00:07:23,818
Hey.

85
00:07:24,902 --> 00:07:27,112
Whoa. The hell you doing?

86
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:29,198
Knock it off right now.

87
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:32,452
Hey!

88
00:07:33,494 --> 00:07:36,997
I'm so sorry. No cameras allowed.
Mind if I take a look inside your bag too?

89
00:07:36,998 --> 00:07:38,166
Here.

90
00:07:39,625 --> 00:07:40,668
Let go!

91
00:07:42,253 --> 00:07:43,588
Let go!

92
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:46,882
What the hell are you doing?

93
00:07:46,883 --> 00:07:49,469
Let go this instant!

94
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:00,730
- Ah, what the hell?
- Hey!

95
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:02,982
Hey, stop!

96
00:08:03,566 --> 00:08:05,442
Wait.

97
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:08,361
Stop! Idiots.

98
00:08:08,362 --> 00:08:10,281
- Sorry, sir!
- Hey, stop!

99
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:17,204
Stop running!

100
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:18,623
Hey!

101
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:21,667
Who's that?

102
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:24,962
- Hey.
- Hey.

103
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:35,932
Hey, whoa!

104
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:43,523
Hey! Someone call the cops.
That guy's crazy!

105
00:08:47,818 --> 00:08:49,111
Watch out!

106
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:55,660
Stop running!

107
00:09:09,131 --> 00:09:10,049
Oh, my God!

108
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:19,350
I got you!

109
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:42,247
Hey, careful.

110
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:44,458
Wait, you're Korean?

111
00:09:51,132 --> 00:09:52,425
Hold on.

112
00:09:53,175 --> 00:09:54,427
Huh?

113
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,684
Turn around! Right now!

114
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:06,564
Sir! Are you okay?

115
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:14,070
TOKYO METROPOLITAN
POLICE DEPARTMENT

116
00:10:14,071 --> 00:10:17,116
INVESTIGATION DIVISION 1

117
00:10:24,248 --> 00:10:26,042
- Excuse me, pardon.
- Morning.

118
00:10:27,418 --> 00:10:29,544
- Morning, everyone.
- Hi, hello.

119
00:10:29,545 --> 00:10:32,214
Inose's team pulled another all-nighter.

120
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:35,176
They worked all night?

121
00:10:36,093 --> 00:10:37,303
How's the case going?

122
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:47,521
You were taking photos of the crime scene.

123
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:59,450
What's this camera for, huh?

124
00:11:01,035 --> 00:11:03,203
So you're not gonna cooperate with us?

125
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:05,915
Answer the detective right now!

126
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:08,584
Hold on, Sagawa.

127
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:10,961
Sorry?

128
00:11:15,841 --> 00:11:16,842
Oh.

129
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:24,933
I'll let it slide this time,
but don't draw your weapon unless ordered.

130
00:11:24,934 --> 00:11:27,353
Right. Sorry.

131
00:11:27,853 --> 00:11:29,521
So, Korean.

132
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:33,734
I've been up all night 'cause of you.
You know how cruel that is?

133
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,239
You must be the ace here.

134
00:11:43,285 --> 00:11:44,829
And it's obvious you're the rookie.

135
00:11:46,872 --> 00:11:49,082
What did you just say? Huh, Korean?

136
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:51,043
You killed her. Didn't you?

137
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:53,754
Didn't you? Say something!

138
00:12:00,219 --> 00:12:01,262
So what is it?

139
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:05,015
What are you hiding?

140
00:12:07,059 --> 00:12:08,477
What the hell are y...

141
00:12:15,192 --> 00:12:20,531
I apologize for how unprofessionally my
subordinates have treated you today, sir.

142
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:25,577
Please forgive us, Inspector Kim.

143
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:28,830
Hey! What the hell were you two thinking?

144
00:12:28,831 --> 00:12:30,082
Sorry.

145
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:33,377
- Here.
- Huh.

146
00:12:34,795 --> 00:12:36,880
He's a special investigator from Korea.

147
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:37,964
INTL. COOPERATION REQUEST

148
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:39,758
Are you serious?

149
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:41,509
Korean police have sent over

150
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:43,429
an official statement of cooperation.

151
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:46,973
Sagawa, go set up the conference room.

152
00:12:46,974 --> 00:12:47,975
Yes, sir.

153
00:12:58,402 --> 00:12:59,820
Uh...

154
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:02,573
Allow me to introduce myself.

155
00:13:03,741 --> 00:13:07,161
I'm Detective Kim Seok from Seoul Police's
Mobile Investigation Unit.

156
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:13,375
You mean you really are a detective?

157
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:19,006
Then why didn't you just say so?

158
00:13:20,132 --> 00:13:21,842
Why did you run?

159
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:26,346
I just wanted to see
how Japanese cops treat Koreans.

160
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:27,431
That a problem?

161
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:30,600
Hmm...

162
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:33,813
Whatever. I was looking for
the suspect's escape route.

163
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:36,189
Looking for the escape--

164
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:40,109
Yes. I was simply looking for
the escape route, not running away.

165
00:13:40,110 --> 00:13:41,529
Hmm...

166
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:42,905
Mmm.

167
00:13:43,656 --> 00:13:45,865
I don't think we're gonna get along.

168
00:13:45,866 --> 00:13:47,243
You don't? How come?

169
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:51,288
Are detectives
not allowed at crime scenes?

170
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:02,632
So you do know Japanese after all?

171
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:04,677
Ah. Oh.

172
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:07,638
- When needed.
- When needed?

173
00:14:09,473 --> 00:14:11,015
You a wise guy?

174
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:14,311
Inose! Back off now.

175
00:14:17,898 --> 00:14:19,608
Mm. Mm-mmm.

176
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:25,823
We had a similar murder in Korea recently.

177
00:14:27,157 --> 00:14:29,284
The victim's name was Park In-gyu.

178
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:31,912
He went by Cindy. Thirty-eight years old.

179
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:36,000
He was a known cross-dresser
in the nightlife community.

180
00:14:37,042 --> 00:14:40,004
As you can see,
the body was arranged in a similar manner.

181
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:43,048
Like a work of art,
displayed for an audience.

182
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:47,261
The victim's joints were bent backwards
in the opposite directions,

183
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:51,348
and traces of a psychotropic drug
were found in his blood.

184
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:55,101
It's called Speed K,
a new form of methamphetamine.

185
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:59,230
Speed K has become very popular
in Tokyo as of late.

186
00:14:59,231 --> 00:15:01,482
And it's also spread to Korea.

187
00:15:01,483 --> 00:15:05,195
As you can imagine, the Korean government
is keeping a close eye on it.

188
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:08,740
We did find out
that Park In-gyu had come to Shinjuku

189
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:10,241
to get his hands on this Speed K.

190
00:15:10,242 --> 00:15:12,201
That's why I was at the crime scene.

191
00:15:12,202 --> 00:15:14,830
<i>My plan had been to simply investigate.</i>

192
00:15:15,789 --> 00:15:18,708
<i>But while doing so,
I discovered a body with broken limbs.</i>

193
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:20,419
<i>Just like Park In-gyu's.</i>

194
00:15:22,212 --> 00:15:23,129
Generally speaking...

195
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:24,714
Just by coincidence?

196
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:25,840
...crimes of passion,

197
00:15:25,841 --> 00:15:27,759
the murder scene tends
to feature heavy amounts...

198
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:30,345
Time to crank up
your managing skills, huh?

199
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:31,596
I'm sorry.

200
00:15:31,597 --> 00:15:36,143
Both murder scenes were immaculate.
Almost like, uh, an art display.

201
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:38,771
And finally,

202
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:42,482
if you look at this phrase
that was written at the scene

203
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:44,109
of Park In-gyu's murder,

204
00:15:45,235 --> 00:15:48,405
you'll see it was also written in blood,
just like in Shinjuku.

205
00:15:50,282 --> 00:15:52,700
"One fear gives birth to endless fears,

206
00:15:52,701 --> 00:15:54,954
but its methods shall remain hidden."

207
00:15:55,788 --> 00:15:57,206
They say the same thing.

208
00:15:59,083 --> 00:16:00,793
So they both say the same thing?

209
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:04,046
Does that mean
there could be more than one perpetrator?

210
00:16:04,713 --> 00:16:07,007
So what's the point? What are you saying?

211
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:10,259
That this case spans
across two different countries?

212
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:12,721
You're here 'cause you think
the suspect is Korean?

213
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:19,687
In Korean,
our words have spaces between them.

214
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:22,146
But as you can see here,

215
00:16:22,147 --> 00:16:24,525
there are no spaces between the words.

216
00:16:26,777 --> 00:16:29,988
Therefore, the Korean
National Intelligence Service

217
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:31,281
has concluded

218
00:16:32,616 --> 00:16:33,826
the murderer

219
00:16:34,952 --> 00:16:35,869
is Japanese.

220
00:16:40,874 --> 00:16:42,333
- Sagawa, Mikitani.
- Yes.

221
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:44,919
- Go get the forensics report immediately.
- Right away.

222
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,671
Okamoto, Hosaka.

223
00:16:46,672 --> 00:16:49,716
Search for all the witnesses
who were near the crime scene.

224
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:50,842
Yes, sir.

225
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:52,885
We should look into similar cases.

226
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:54,013
Good idea.

227
00:16:54,722 --> 00:16:57,224
Gotta check the junkies, what'd I say?

228
00:17:00,686 --> 00:17:02,563
And as for you...

229
00:17:05,274 --> 00:17:06,274
Hmm?

230
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:08,652
...you're in charge of the Korean.

231
00:17:11,196 --> 00:17:12,156
Huh?

232
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,825
- For real? Come on.
- Good work today.

233
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:17,201
- You too.
- Excuse me.

234
00:17:17,202 --> 00:17:18,244
Excuse me.

235
00:17:18,245 --> 00:17:19,163
Sorry.

236
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:24,084
Hey, Korean.

237
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:29,882
You can understand what I'm saying, right?

238
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:34,803
You're somewhat of a loner, aren't you?

239
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:37,181
That's why they stuck you with me.

240
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:43,228
I've never met a detective
who wasn't a loner.

241
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:46,857
Anyway, can we at least agree

242
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:49,068
to speak in Japanese?

243
00:17:49,943 --> 00:17:51,361
And why should I do that?

244
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:56,158
Because you think it's a better language?

245
00:17:56,658 --> 00:17:57,993
Mmm...

246
00:18:01,205 --> 00:18:02,706
I know Korean too.

247
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:05,793
A little.

248
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:07,795
<i>Winter Sonata.</i>

249
00:18:08,837 --> 00:18:11,172
Yonsama. See?

250
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:13,217
It's best if I keep this brief.

251
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:16,595
I don't wanna work with a partner either.

252
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:20,599
Mmm.

253
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:28,023
What the hell is his deal?

254
00:18:31,777 --> 00:18:34,571
God, he's a pain in the ass.

255
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:07,854
NEW MESSAGE

256
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:09,647
YOUR MOTHER'S BEEN
QUITE DELIRIOUS LATELY.

257
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:11,567
IT MIGHT HELP IF YOU STOPPED BY.

258
00:19:59,072 --> 00:20:00,657
Seok.

259
00:20:03,118 --> 00:20:04,369
Kim Seok.

260
00:20:08,874 --> 00:20:10,375
Kim Seok.

261
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:13,378
Do not fear...

262
00:20:26,892 --> 00:20:30,145
SHINJUKU KABUKICHO

263
00:20:33,398 --> 00:20:35,149
- What time do they close?
- 2:00, I think.

264
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:36,651
- S'up, guys?
- Or maybe 3:00.

265
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:38,027
Any of you seen this girl?

266
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:40,363
- Huh? Who? Wow, she's so cute!
- Her? Haven't seen her.

267
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:42,156
Ew, no way. She looks like my mom.

268
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:43,658
- How old are you?
- Uh, 20.

269
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:45,618
- You wanna come party with us?
- 20? Yeah, right.

270
00:20:45,619 --> 00:20:47,537
- Hey, man! Hey, come on!
- Aw, come on!

271
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:50,706
Hey, guys. Have you seen this girl?

272
00:20:50,707 --> 00:20:52,458
- Whoa!
- What do you want?

273
00:20:52,459 --> 00:20:54,043
I think I know her.

274
00:20:54,044 --> 00:20:55,670
- For real?
- She looks pretty hot.

275
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:58,382
Yeah. I'm messing with you.

276
00:20:59,675 --> 00:21:01,842
So you're funny, is that it?
You think this is a joke?

277
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:02,886
Wanna try that again?

278
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:17,943
DO NOT ENTER

279
00:21:25,158 --> 00:21:27,285
- Can you get more of this stuff?
- This is so sick.

280
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:29,954
You know I'm good for it.
Don't be like that.

281
00:21:29,955 --> 00:21:32,498
You ladies having fun?

282
00:21:32,499 --> 00:21:34,333
- Hey, so, have you seen...
- Who is this?

283
00:21:34,334 --> 00:21:37,670
Yeah, I'm just some gross old guy.
You know this girl? She was murdered.

284
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:38,879
- By who?
- That's so messed up!

285
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:40,172
- She was killed?
- You know her?

286
00:21:40,173 --> 00:21:43,343
- Yeah. She was.
- Wow! She's adorable.

287
00:21:44,678 --> 00:21:46,846
- Wait a minute. Hold on.
- That's so creepy. Who is this guy?

288
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:47,847
She looks like Aki.

289
00:21:47,848 --> 00:21:49,557
- What? You think?
- Aki?

290
00:21:49,558 --> 00:21:50,766
No way. Aki? Really?

291
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:52,226
- Yeah, look.
- No, you're crazy.

292
00:21:52,227 --> 00:21:53,894
She's got a mole right under her eye.

293
00:21:53,895 --> 00:21:56,105
- No way. It's a coincidence.
- It's Aki!

294
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:58,733
Tell me about this. Her name is Aki?

295
00:21:58,734 --> 00:22:00,192
- She's a friend?
- Sort of.

296
00:22:00,193 --> 00:22:02,111
Her name is Aki Miyashita.

297
00:22:02,112 --> 00:22:04,030
- We only hung out a few times.
- Yeah, that so?

298
00:22:04,031 --> 00:22:07,491
Whenever she'd get drunk,
she'd start crying, saying things like,

299
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:10,202
"I miss my mommy,"
and, "This sucks, I wanna go home."

300
00:22:10,203 --> 00:22:12,997
- She was so annoying. What a baby.
- Oh, yeah? Oh.

301
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:14,415
I mean, come on.

302
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:16,459
When was the last time you saw her?

303
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:18,794
Uh, last time I saw her was...

304
00:22:18,795 --> 00:22:21,464
- Uh-oh.
- I think it was last Saturday.

305
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:24,175
I saw her at the karaoke bar,
but she was with Takahashi,

306
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:25,968
so I didn't say hi or anything.

307
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:27,053
Takahashi?

308
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:28,805
- Hey, hey, knock it off.
- Oh, uh...

309
00:22:30,182 --> 00:22:32,683
Don't talk about him.

310
00:22:32,684 --> 00:22:33,934
You brought him up!

311
00:22:33,935 --> 00:22:38,356
All right, enough! Get out!
So long! Bye-bye, mister!

312
00:22:38,357 --> 00:22:40,816
- Yeah.
- Bye, buddy! See ya!

313
00:22:40,817 --> 00:22:43,152
All right, I got you. Okay. Thank you.

314
00:22:43,153 --> 00:22:44,154
Bye!

315
00:22:44,654 --> 00:22:47,406
What the hell?

316
00:22:47,407 --> 00:22:48,992
Get off me!

317
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:51,661
What the hell are you doing?

318
00:22:52,829 --> 00:22:55,122
- Get your dirty hands off of me!
- Speed K.

319
00:22:55,123 --> 00:22:57,417
Did this Takahashi get it for you?
Where is he?

320
00:22:58,001 --> 00:23:00,961
Let go! Stop it, you creep!

321
00:23:00,962 --> 00:23:02,464
Where's your friend, huh?

322
00:23:09,429 --> 00:23:12,849
I gotta find me
some new clientele. Business sucks.

323
00:23:14,684 --> 00:23:16,019
Takahashi Shoma.

324
00:23:16,645 --> 00:23:17,604
Huh?

325
00:23:18,230 --> 00:23:19,439
Who the hell are you?

326
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:27,279
Guess it is you.

327
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:30,157
A Josenjing? Huh?

328
00:23:30,158 --> 00:23:32,411
The hell you want from me? Huh?

329
00:23:33,245 --> 00:23:34,579
This was self-defense.

330
00:23:37,082 --> 00:23:39,251
You goddamn...

331
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:44,256
Joseon hasn't existed
for over a hundred years, okay?

332
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:47,174
Because of you people.

333
00:23:47,175 --> 00:23:49,219
Hey, try not to move.

334
00:23:49,928 --> 00:23:52,305
- Or it'll break.
- Shut up, Josenjing!

335
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:55,058
What's that guy doing?

336
00:23:57,185 --> 00:23:58,311
Do you know him?

337
00:23:58,812 --> 00:24:01,731
No, I don't! What are you talking about?

338
00:24:04,943 --> 00:24:06,236
Hey, Korean.

339
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:10,907
What the...

340
00:24:11,658 --> 00:24:13,743
What exactly are you...

341
00:24:14,744 --> 00:24:16,496
What are you doing here?

342
00:24:17,706 --> 00:24:20,332
The victim bought drugs
from this guy in Shinjuku.

343
00:24:20,333 --> 00:24:23,545
- What are you talking about?
- The Korean victim, Park In-gyu.

344
00:24:25,672 --> 00:24:27,673
- Oh, that's Takahashi.
- Yeah.

345
00:24:27,674 --> 00:24:28,842
Get off!

346
00:24:29,384 --> 00:24:31,302
Let's go! Just add it to the tab.

347
00:24:31,303 --> 00:24:32,219
I'll pay next time!

348
00:24:32,220 --> 00:24:34,722
- Yo, Akira.
- Let's go! Where to next?

349
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:37,224
- Akira! Help!
- Who wants a drink? This way!

350
00:24:37,225 --> 00:24:39,810
- Hey, man, help me!
- The hell's all this?

351
00:24:39,811 --> 00:24:41,729
These bastards attacked me!

352
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:42,938
And who are they?

353
00:24:42,939 --> 00:24:45,858
How should I know?
Some Josenjing bastards.

354
00:24:45,859 --> 00:24:47,360
Hey, there.

355
00:24:48,069 --> 00:24:49,905
We're police, you idiots.

356
00:24:51,031 --> 00:24:52,699
You think I give a shit?

357
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:55,534
Doesn't give you the right
to shake him down.

358
00:24:55,535 --> 00:24:58,037
You're screwed now.

359
00:24:58,038 --> 00:24:58,997
Yeah.

360
00:24:59,498 --> 00:25:01,917
Whoa, whoa now. Easy.

361
00:25:02,501 --> 00:25:05,253
Besides, there's no way
a Josenjing would be a cop.

362
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:07,422
This is getting on my nerves.

363
00:25:18,892 --> 00:25:21,561
Oh, my God! Watch out!

364
00:25:38,828 --> 00:25:40,080
Ah, you flinched.

365
00:25:45,585 --> 00:25:48,213
That's enough now. Put it down.

366
00:26:05,939 --> 00:26:06,939
Oh, my God.

367
00:26:06,940 --> 00:26:09,276
That was incredible. Did you see that?

368
00:26:09,943 --> 00:26:11,820
- That was insane!
- My God!

369
00:26:15,615 --> 00:26:17,491
Ah, get off me! Ow!

370
00:26:17,492 --> 00:26:20,662
What are you doing? Let me go! What the...

371
00:26:22,539 --> 00:26:23,999
Untie me right now!

372
00:26:24,541 --> 00:26:26,126
Oh, come on, man. Let me go!

373
00:26:27,294 --> 00:26:29,587
Okay, so, you killed her, right?

374
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:31,381
And you killed him, didn't you?

375
00:26:32,674 --> 00:26:34,718
Huh? What are you talking about?

376
00:26:35,260 --> 00:26:37,220
Wait. Aki?

377
00:26:38,221 --> 00:26:40,056
You're saying... You're saying she's dead?

378
00:26:41,057 --> 00:26:44,852
No way. You think I did it? Come on!
What reason would I have to kill her?

379
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:48,147
We have a witness
who saw you with Aki Miyashita

380
00:26:48,148 --> 00:26:50,357
just a few days before she was found dead.

381
00:26:50,358 --> 00:26:51,692
Ah...

382
00:26:51,693 --> 00:26:53,068
Are you for real?

383
00:26:53,069 --> 00:26:54,570
She was crying and wouldn't shut up,

384
00:26:54,571 --> 00:26:56,780
but I swear, all I did was
knock her around a little!

385
00:26:56,781 --> 00:27:00,492
- I'm telling you, I did not kill her!
- If you didn't kill her, then who did?

386
00:27:00,493 --> 00:27:01,536
Huh?

387
00:27:02,078 --> 00:27:03,037
Hmm?

388
00:27:03,038 --> 00:27:04,622
Now is your chance.

389
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:07,334
All you gotta do
is tell us what you remember.

390
00:27:09,044 --> 00:27:10,920
Of course, unless you want
your limbs broken too.

391
00:27:11,963 --> 00:27:13,506
All of my... What?

392
00:27:17,969 --> 00:27:19,428
Uh...

393
00:27:19,429 --> 00:27:22,598
Are you saying Aki's limbs
were all broken when you found her?

394
00:27:22,599 --> 00:27:23,725
Mm-hmm.

395
00:27:25,268 --> 00:27:26,394
My God.

396
00:27:28,563 --> 00:27:31,982
He did it. It was him, the photographer.

397
00:27:31,983 --> 00:27:32,984
Who?

398
00:27:36,071 --> 00:27:37,280
A photographer?

399
00:27:38,782 --> 00:27:40,450
<i>Oh. That guy?</i>

400
00:27:42,786 --> 00:27:46,122
There was a rumor a few years back.
It was going around the street gangs.

401
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:50,376
Supposedly, there was this hit man
who was taking gigs from the yakuza.

402
00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:53,170
He'd always take a photo
whenever he finished a job.

403
00:27:53,171 --> 00:27:57,717
<i>But there's nothing yet connecting him
to either of these murders.</i>

404
00:28:00,637 --> 00:28:03,347
No drugs were ever found in his victims.

405
00:28:03,348 --> 00:28:06,725
Not to mention,
his victims had been sexually assaulted.

406
00:28:06,726 --> 00:28:09,728
Most importantly, these bodies
were disposed of in different manners.

407
00:28:09,729 --> 00:28:11,897
The MO is completely different
from Shinjuku.

408
00:28:11,898 --> 00:28:13,065
<i>Why do you ask?</i>

409
00:28:13,066 --> 00:28:14,150
Uh...

410
00:28:14,818 --> 00:28:18,613
So, then where exactly
is this hit-man-photographer now?

411
00:28:19,114 --> 00:28:20,989
<i>Well, he was never arrested.</i>

412
00:28:20,990 --> 00:28:24,326
<i>It ended up being a yakuza turf war,
way out of our depth.</i>

413
00:28:24,327 --> 00:28:25,745
<i>But we did identify him.</i>

414
00:28:26,329 --> 00:28:28,664
Even so, the man was like a ghost.

415
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:32,126
It's like...
It's like the guy just disappeared.

416
00:28:32,127 --> 00:28:35,171
<i>There's gotta be something we can use.
Come on!</i>

417
00:28:35,672 --> 00:28:37,590
Look, just keep digging, okay?

418
00:28:44,973 --> 00:28:47,058
Come on!

419
00:28:49,519 --> 00:28:53,313
Hey! Hey! Hey, you can't just leave! Yo!

420
00:28:53,314 --> 00:28:54,857
Where are you going?

421
00:28:54,858 --> 00:28:58,069
- Come back and untie me! Goddamn pigs!
- We'd better start looking into this guy.

422
00:28:58,695 --> 00:29:02,990
This photographer-hit-man's
Japanese name is Mikogami.

423
00:29:02,991 --> 00:29:05,784
His Korean name is Kim Chang-tae.

424
00:29:05,785 --> 00:29:07,495
He's a Korean in Japan.

425
00:29:08,163 --> 00:29:11,374
No one has been able to find him
for the past couple of years.

426
00:29:13,793 --> 00:29:17,172
Maybe he moved to a different country,
changed identities...

427
00:29:17,964 --> 00:29:20,842
Since he's Korean,
he might've just gone there.

428
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:25,805
Wherever he is,
he would have continued killing.

429
00:29:29,893 --> 00:29:32,020
Someone like him wouldn't be able to stop.

430
00:29:33,897 --> 00:29:37,525
You're saying he would have kept
right on killing like nothing changed?

431
00:29:41,154 --> 00:29:43,323
There's only two ways
he could have stopped.

432
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:46,743
Either he died, or he got caught.

433
00:29:47,243 --> 00:29:48,828
Mikogami

434
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:51,164
is in prison?

435
00:29:52,665 --> 00:29:53,708
Perhaps.

436
00:29:55,293 --> 00:29:57,295
Ah, no. There's no way.

437
00:29:58,254 --> 00:29:59,671
If he was in prison,

438
00:29:59,672 --> 00:30:02,383
then he would have turned up
in our system long ago.

439
00:30:03,176 --> 00:30:06,221
You said he's a Korean living in Japan,
a Zainichi.

440
00:30:07,972 --> 00:30:10,308
So maybe he kept his Korean citizenship.

441
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:13,144
That's why the Japanese police
couldn't find him.

442
00:30:15,522 --> 00:30:18,316
Mikogami Sota is actually then...

443
00:30:20,401 --> 00:30:21,611
Kim Chang-tae?

444
00:30:40,046 --> 00:30:41,004
KANTO FOREIGNERS' PRISON

445
00:30:41,005 --> 00:30:43,675
Okay, so if he is in here...

446
00:30:44,259 --> 00:30:45,927
Let's just see if he is first.

447
00:31:08,241 --> 00:31:10,827
So I'm guessing the yakuza blinded you.

448
00:31:11,911 --> 00:31:14,122
A blind photographer.

449
00:31:14,956 --> 00:31:17,166
Not everything is so black and white.

450
00:31:21,045 --> 00:31:23,338
Two of you, huh?

451
00:31:23,339 --> 00:31:26,174
So, you operated
under the name Kim Chang-tae, right?

452
00:31:26,175 --> 00:31:27,552
Not Mikogami.

453
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:32,056
The yakuza
are foaming at the mouth to kill you.

454
00:31:32,849 --> 00:31:35,602
You get yourself locked up on purpose?

455
00:31:36,519 --> 00:31:38,313
Is this about Shinjuku?

456
00:31:41,316 --> 00:31:42,357
What did you just say?

457
00:31:42,358 --> 00:31:45,986
It's true. The methodology
is close to my past work,

458
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:47,946
but I'm afraid I was in here, officers.

459
00:31:47,947 --> 00:31:51,408
So I imagine you thought
someone must have been copying me.

460
00:31:51,409 --> 00:31:53,201
So you decided to visit

461
00:31:53,202 --> 00:31:56,205
to see if you could get
any kind of lead, right?

462
00:31:58,958 --> 00:32:00,043
Am I wrong?

463
00:32:01,586 --> 00:32:04,631
You came here
already knowing I didn't do it.

464
00:32:06,341 --> 00:32:07,799
A copycat.

465
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:09,218
A Korean one?

466
00:32:10,094 --> 00:32:11,220
However,

467
00:32:12,430 --> 00:32:14,599
this copycat is better than you,
I'm afraid.

468
00:32:15,558 --> 00:32:16,391
What?

469
00:32:16,392 --> 00:32:19,187
He's got much more finesse.
His kills are works of art.

470
00:32:20,980 --> 00:32:23,775
You just butchered a few people
and twisted their limbs around a bit.

471
00:32:24,817 --> 00:32:28,279
The Shinjuku killer was meticulous.
He crafted masterpieces.

472
00:32:29,072 --> 00:32:30,156
Just my opinion.

473
00:32:31,908 --> 00:32:36,037
He's more adventurous,
more imaginative, more creative than you.

474
00:32:37,372 --> 00:32:39,499
You sure you didn't copy him instead?

475
00:32:42,669 --> 00:32:45,505
Shut your mouth, or I'll shut it for you.

476
00:32:47,632 --> 00:32:50,426
What did you just say to me? Say it again!

477
00:32:55,807 --> 00:32:57,892
Hey, hey! Are you okay?

478
00:32:58,518 --> 00:33:00,894
Hey! Hey!

479
00:33:00,895 --> 00:33:03,146
Get up. What's going on here?

480
00:33:03,147 --> 00:33:04,982
Can you hear me?

481
00:33:04,983 --> 00:33:07,442
- Hey! Just breathe. Relax.
- I need backup.

482
00:33:07,443 --> 00:33:09,821
You might not be the culprit
for these murders,

483
00:33:11,030 --> 00:33:13,574
but Shinjuku is the original, not you.

484
00:33:15,451 --> 00:33:16,661
He did it first.

485
00:33:17,412 --> 00:33:19,414
- I need help!
- Tell me. Am I wrong?

486
00:33:45,356 --> 00:33:46,858
You're a funny guy.

487
00:33:47,775 --> 00:33:48,985
Hey, wait.

488
00:33:49,652 --> 00:33:50,820
Fill me in here.

489
00:34:00,788 --> 00:34:02,790
The original, the one you copied.

490
00:34:06,252 --> 00:34:07,295
Who was he?

491
00:34:15,219 --> 00:34:16,637
You ever even met him?

492
00:34:18,556 --> 00:34:19,682
The original?

493
00:34:24,604 --> 00:34:27,940
I have no idea
if Shinjuku is the original or not.

494
00:34:28,441 --> 00:34:30,151
But I can tell you one thing.

495
00:34:30,902 --> 00:34:33,613
There were bodies with twisted limbs

496
00:34:34,113 --> 00:34:36,448
a long time before I did it.

497
00:34:36,449 --> 00:34:37,784
Or Shinjuku.

498
00:34:40,203 --> 00:34:42,413
Did I meet them? Don't make me laugh.

499
00:34:42,914 --> 00:34:46,042
I was inspired
by reading the old newspaper headlines.

500
00:34:48,711 --> 00:34:50,755
Does that disappoint you, officers?

501
00:34:56,469 --> 00:35:00,056
Sorry, I have no idea
what the guy's name was.

502
00:35:00,556 --> 00:35:03,683
It's been so long that I assumed by now

503
00:35:03,684 --> 00:35:05,561
they were dead or caught.

504
00:35:06,854 --> 00:35:08,231
Did they resurrect?

505
00:35:11,192 --> 00:35:13,486
And you two are gonna try to catch him?

506
00:35:15,905 --> 00:35:18,116
Hey, guard!

507
00:35:19,075 --> 00:35:20,952
Get me out!

508
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:30,336
Well, then,
wish the best of luck to you both.

509
00:35:34,132 --> 00:35:36,175
Hey. Wait!

510
00:35:40,138 --> 00:35:43,182
You may be a killer yourself,
but that doesn't make you an expert.

511
00:35:44,976 --> 00:35:47,853
You're pathetic. You're just a criminal
who will die in this prison.

512
00:35:47,854 --> 00:35:49,480
Don't forget that.

513
00:35:52,108 --> 00:35:55,068
I guess
you weren't told everything, after all.

514
00:35:55,069 --> 00:35:56,571
Huh, detective?

515
00:36:22,722 --> 00:36:24,557
Where are you taking me this late?

516
00:36:26,934 --> 00:36:30,146
Just be patient.
I wanna go home too, you know.

517
00:36:51,667 --> 00:36:55,087
I'm so very sorry for your loss.

518
00:36:56,631 --> 00:36:59,050
As police,
we should have protected your daughter.

519
00:36:59,675 --> 00:37:02,386
I sincerely apologize for our failure.

520
00:37:03,387 --> 00:37:04,972
Please know I'm so very sorry.

521
00:37:13,147 --> 00:37:15,566
But rest assured,
we will catch whoever did this.

522
00:37:23,241 --> 00:37:25,201
I too sincerely apologize.

523
00:37:28,955 --> 00:37:32,166
I failed as a father.
I did not raise my daughter right.

524
00:37:36,963 --> 00:37:38,506
She was a troublemaker.

525
00:37:40,508 --> 00:37:43,219
That girl never showed any gratitude
to her parents.

526
00:37:45,888 --> 00:37:48,015
Running away, doing drugs.

527
00:37:49,016 --> 00:37:50,142
She was

528
00:37:50,726 --> 00:37:52,812
a disgrace to our family.

529
00:37:55,398 --> 00:37:57,608
Deep down, I always had a feeling...

530
00:37:59,443 --> 00:38:01,445
that this would be her fate.

531
00:38:03,823 --> 00:38:06,450
So I'm sorry that you came all this way.

532
00:38:07,118 --> 00:38:08,410
We're so sorry for the trouble.

533
00:38:08,411 --> 00:38:10,413
We're sorry for our failure.

534
00:38:11,998 --> 00:38:14,207
We are so sorry.

535
00:38:14,208 --> 00:38:16,710
Please. Please know how sorry we are.

536
00:38:16,711 --> 00:38:18,921
We are just so sorry.

537
00:38:21,340 --> 00:38:23,049
We're so, so sorry.

538
00:38:23,050 --> 00:38:24,884
Please forgive us.

539
00:38:24,885 --> 00:38:27,262
We're sorry
for making you come all this way.

540
00:38:27,263 --> 00:38:29,973
- We've caused such grief.
- Forgive us.

541
00:38:29,974 --> 00:38:32,058
- Um...
- Please forgive us.

542
00:38:32,059 --> 00:38:33,476
Please.

543
00:38:33,477 --> 00:38:35,479
- We beg for your forgiveness.
- Stop apologizing.

544
00:38:36,605 --> 00:38:39,859
That's enough!
You're asking for our forgiveness?

545
00:38:41,068 --> 00:38:42,694
Your daughter has been murdered.

546
00:38:42,695 --> 00:38:45,156
Why are you acting
like she did something wrong?

547
00:38:46,866 --> 00:38:48,367
She was your daughter.

548
00:38:49,118 --> 00:38:51,704
She still had her whole life ahead of her!

549
00:38:53,581 --> 00:38:55,207
She cried out for you,

550
00:38:56,250 --> 00:38:57,918
right up until her final breath.

551
00:38:58,669 --> 00:39:01,088
She cried she wanted to go home.

552
00:39:03,382 --> 00:39:05,134
So stop apologizing.

553
00:39:06,427 --> 00:39:09,138
Don't you dare apologize for her
like that, understand?

554
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:20,608
Come on.

555
00:39:52,056 --> 00:39:53,474
Hey, Korean.

556
00:39:56,352 --> 00:40:00,564
Is there seriously any point in trying
to make this shitty world a better place?

557
00:40:05,319 --> 00:40:06,404
Listen.

558
00:40:08,697 --> 00:40:10,324
Don't take this the wrong way.

559
00:40:13,828 --> 00:40:15,955
I'd like it
if you didn't call me "Korean."

560
00:40:17,957 --> 00:40:19,291
Call me by my name.

561
00:40:20,126 --> 00:40:21,293
Just Kim Seok.

562
00:40:21,919 --> 00:40:23,254
Or Detective Kim.

563
00:40:23,754 --> 00:40:24,797
Hmm.

564
00:40:27,007 --> 00:40:28,384
Sure, understood.

565
00:40:30,511 --> 00:40:33,264
I'm sorry, Detective Kim.

566
00:40:37,059 --> 00:40:38,060
Now what?

567
00:40:41,313 --> 00:40:42,648
You gonna just give up?

568
00:40:52,241 --> 00:40:54,368
That's it. I've had enough for one day.

569
00:41:03,836 --> 00:41:05,087
Can I get a light?

570
00:41:18,392 --> 00:41:19,267
So...

571
00:41:19,268 --> 00:41:22,395
It makes less and less sense
the longer I think about it.

572
00:41:22,396 --> 00:41:26,649
You came to investigate a murder
that was committed in Korea.

573
00:41:26,650 --> 00:41:31,405
And just like that, you just so happened
to find an identical one?

574
00:41:34,074 --> 00:41:35,075
Seriously?

575
00:41:37,495 --> 00:41:39,370
What, are you psychic or something?

576
00:41:39,371 --> 00:41:42,500
And what were all those questions
about the "original?"

577
00:41:47,213 --> 00:41:48,422
The original.

578
00:41:56,972 --> 00:41:59,683
Remember the old headlines he mentioned?

579
00:42:04,605 --> 00:42:05,898
<i>A long time ago...</i>

580
00:42:08,234 --> 00:42:10,611
<i>back in the '80s, in Korea...</i>

581
00:42:15,741 --> 00:42:18,911
<i>...they found a body, all twisted,
the limbs all broken.</i>

582
00:42:21,830 --> 00:42:22,790
Huh?

583
00:42:25,918 --> 00:42:28,712
That case wasn't the first either.

584
00:42:29,338 --> 00:42:30,422
This one,

585
00:42:32,091 --> 00:42:33,175
it's a pattern.

586
00:42:35,553 --> 00:42:37,555
It's been going on for a long time.

587
00:42:41,892 --> 00:42:45,187
The original killer has indeed returned.
